Z||000000||Dan010||11-01-2001||10:39 AM||||Confussed on which coolant/temp sensor is located where??<BR>86 2.8<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Dan010||11-01-2001||12:17 PM||||Figured it out, was easy when I took time to think about it.<BR>But thanks all the same||||reg||1
Z||000002||Dan010||11-01-2001||09:21 PM||||Well I thought I had it all figured out, but I was wrong!!!!<BR>Found the sensor for the gauge and light,<BR>sensor for the fan/relay, found another<BR>sensor right next to this sensor, but has a pink/white and tan wires going to/coming from it. Haynes book plus new sensor indicates yellow and black for the engine coolant temperature sensor. cant seem to locate it HELP!!!! where is it!!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000003||reddog||11-01-2001||09:51 PM||||It's under the thermostat housing on the right hand side of the engine(Battery side). You'll have to remove the egr vacuum solenoid. Careful though, there is a plug that is threaded that the coolant temp. sensor screws into. If you unscrew that one by mistake you'll lose about a quart or two of coolant.By the way, there are several other switches in that area so be careful. The one you are looking for is directly under the thermostat housing and is mounted horizontally not vertically into the block!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Cutout_1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Dan010||11-01-2001||10:00 PM||||THANKS!!!!<BR>Will go give it a try!!!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Dan010||11-01-2001||11:58 PM||||Found it, replaced it, Thanks!!!!<BR>She is running so much better, starting to work properly, cold idles at 1500 rpm then idles down to around 1000. pretty steady, once in awhile will bounce around, up to 1300 then settle back to 1000rpm, may take the throttle body off and give it a good cleaning, still need to check the timing.<BR>Checked radiator relay and fan, works fine now. Will tackle trans mounts this weekend, allready replaced motor mount and dog bone, could not get one bolt out of the back trans mount bracket, got a 6 point socket to see if this might help. any suggestions????<BR>Have learn a lot from reading and asking all of you for help. Again I say "THANKS" ||||reg||1
